  "description": "Canonical build → release → tag → publish procedure for the @delorenj/mcp-server-trello repo. Use when cutting a release, bumping the version, tagging, or publishing to npm / the MCP registry — triggers: \"cut a release\", \"release 1.x.y\", \"ship a new version\", \"bump the version\", \"publish to npm\", \"publish to the MCP registry\", \"tag the release\", \"how do I release this\". Codifies the FOUR version-bearing literals that must move in lockstep (package.json, server.json ×2, src/index.ts McpServer info) plus CHANGELOG, and the exact GitHub-Actions triggers that make merging a PR the publish event. Do NOT use for generic changelog prose (docs-changelog), cross-repo semver task scaffolding (mise-versioning), or non-release tagging.",
